          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %em Hitchin connection
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hitchin90"}> Hitchin 90
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projectively+flat+connection"} projectively flat connection
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of Riemann surfaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_\Sigma
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            assigns to the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connection"} moduli space of flat connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Loc
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Loc_G(\Sigma)
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+sections"} holomorphic sections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            of the CS theory with respect to the induced Kähler structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Loc
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Loc_G(\Sigma)
            (induced, for abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a{:href => "intermediate+Jacobian#WeilIntermediateJacobian"} Weil complex structure
            and in the general nonabelian case via the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau+theorem"} Donaldson-Uhlenbeck-Yau theorem
          %p
            Therefore the existence and (projective) flatness of the Hitchin connection exhibits the relative independence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            from the choice of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
          %p
            The Hitchin connection is akin to the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} holographic dually
            of the vector bundle of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            A more axiomatic characterization of such projectively flat connections in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functors"} modular functors
            is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Segal88"} Segal 88, prop. 5.4
            %a{:href => "#Segal88"} Segal 88, around (5.9)
            for discussion of how to turn these projectively flat connections into genuine
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
          %p
            Reviews of the Hitchin connection include
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lauridsen10"} Lauridsen 10, section 2
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} AdS3-CFT2 and CS-WZW correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article is
          %ul
            %li#Hitchin90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> Nigel Hitchin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104200841"} Euclid
          %p
            (What is now called the Hitchin connection appears in theorem 3.6 there, its expression in local coordinates is around (3.15). That for abelian gauge group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            the classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+theta+functions"} Riemann theta functions
            constitute the covariantly constant sections of the Hitchin connection in these coordinates is remark 4.12.)
          %p
            More axiomatic/abstract discussion of these projectively flat connections in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functors"} modular functors
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Segal88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              , section 5 of
              %em The definition of conformal field theory
              , preprint, 1988; also in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrike+Tillmann"} Ulrike Tillmann
              (ed.)
              %em Topology, geometry and quantum field theory
              , London Math. Soc. Lect. Note Ser., Vol. 308. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge (2004) 421-577. (
              %a{:href => "https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/segalg/0521540496txt.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p More explicit expressions are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Bert van Geemen,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aise+Johan+de+Jong"} Aise Johan de Jong
              %em On Hitchin’s Connection
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg--geom/9701007"}> arXiv:alg–geom/9701007
              )
          %p A nice review and new concise account is in
          %ul
            %li#Looijenga10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduard+Looijenga"}> Eduard Looijenga
                ,
                %em From WZW models to Modular Functors
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.2245"}> arXiv:1009.2245
                )
            %li#Andersen11
              %p
                Johan Martens
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"} Jørgen Andersen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological quantum field theories and moduli spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://maths.fuglede.dk/noter/tqftms.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            instead of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
              ,
              %em Hitchin’s connection, Toeplitz operators and symmetry invariant deformation quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611126"}> arXiv:math/0611126
              )
          %p
            This also reproduces the original construciton in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            in
          %ul
            %li#AxelrodPietraWitten91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
              , S. Della Pietra,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization of Chern-Simons gauge theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214446565"} EUCLID
          %p
            More details (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+correction"} metaplectic correction
          %ul
            %li#ScheinostSchottenloher96
              Peter Scheinost,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
              = succeed "," do
                %em Metaplectic quantization of the moduli spaces of flat and parabolic bundles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/153753"} web
          %p
            Similar generalization away from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+flat+connections"} moduli spaces of flat connections
            to general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+structure"} Kähler structure
            on them is also in
          %ul
            %li#Lauridsen10
              Lauridsen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Aspects of quantum mathematics – Hitchin connections and the AJ conjecture
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://pure.au.dk/portal/files/41741925/imf_phd_2010_mrl.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Relation between the Hitchin connection and bundles of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Laszlo98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Laszlo"} Yves Laszlo
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hitchin’s and WZW connection are the same
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/NYJM/JDG/archive/vol.49/3_5.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
        .revisedby
